d the general solution to the differential equation $f^{′}(x) + 11x = 0$."}] ["q-16400" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088032 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab721a7c-ebb0-5452-b247-5d3816198bf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx} + (4\\sin x)y = 1 + 3\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084927} {:answer/id #uuid "b319152d-c291-5494-a461-4791daa6c062" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx} + (4\\cos x)y = 1 + 3\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084928} {:answer/id #uuid "c17d0099-f48a-51bc-b6bf-feeec39e8bdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx} + (2\\sin x)y = \\frac{1 + 3\\cos x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084929} {:answer/id #uuid "2a507547-4026-5e0f-ae6c-972cd79efc1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx} + \\frac{1 + 3\\cos x}{2} = (2\\sin x)y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084930} {:answer/id #uuid "606289fa-36e0-57ab-b7c2-57b9dbbb4540" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx} + (2\\sin x)y = 1 + \\frac{3}{2}\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084931}] :answer-field/id #uuid "2e534d32-a3b5-5b67-a30a-d8fb0702e472" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084926} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4bcf009-6fca-5110-8ae8-643678b3cb9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)y=\\frac{1+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401434} {:answer/id #uuid "eb82a4b2-58af-556c-a366-f92624768704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)y=1+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401435} {:answer/id #uuid "f4a26a57-987c-5668-b531-e2f3db2b75bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)y=1+\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401436} {:answer/id #uuid "b6972414-a235-5987-855e-567ba571b605" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)y=1+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401437} {:answer/id #uuid "e08cc03c-cea4-583d-b68b-e5c8622f76e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}=(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401438}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401434} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef647b19-79e2-5b54-b8df-1bf5fe9db9b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401433}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e5c269fd-ead8-50e4-b16e-9d9e9b4a244c" :question/math-academy-id "q-16400" :question/problem "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=1-4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nConverting the given equation to standard form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =1-4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ 2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =1+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}y & ={{\\frac{1+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{1+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}.$"}] ["q-17247" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284688 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "397833d7-9cc6-50ae-8de7-3a5674155a04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2e-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282196} {:answer/id #uuid "8d66fe18-2e0a-548c-a20c-052aa8a29cde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282914} {:answer/id #uuid "cfc41fd0-6fd9-5709-9af2-b2dd6b711472" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283503} {:answer/id #uuid "df2ebee4-e1b4-5f85-bbbc-9c810b46a256" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283637} {:answer/id #uuid "fe32be51-d0ac-5644-92b4-204731798028" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283920}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283637} :answer-field/id #uuid "34cf92cc-bcc5-56af-93bf-714a48258bfc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284027}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5816a349-a320-5d09-93fc-2ee07a9147af" :question/math-academy-id "q-17247" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=2{e}^{x}-3{x}^{2}$, find the slope of the tangent at $x=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, using the addition and the power rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{e}^{x}-3{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{e}^{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}) \\\\  & =2{e}^{x}-3(2x) \\\\  & =2{e}^{x}-6x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={(2{e}^{x}-6x)\\,|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =2{e}^{0}-6\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1-0 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] ["q-17255" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284689 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54ad567a-37aa-5c67-8461-48b832a97b6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282410} {:answer/id #uuid "84f495d5-d4be-5db4-8f35-da2bca8cfe2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282836} {:answer/id #uuid "9e412a36-003f-51b6-80db-13d3f13969a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283068} {:answer/id #uuid "a99e9fb3-9911-531b-94e1-18309a3f6530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283157} {:answer/id #uuid "b8bf7484-ada1-5d36-86d4-7dceaa4a2600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283288}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282410} :answer-field/id #uuid "114801c2-0284-5663-a95f-f2fe249472cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283967}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a7bb16ef-b727-58e4-9164-1a907f3660c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-17255" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=11{e}^{x}+8{x}^{2}-12x-20$, find the slope of the tangent at $x=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the addition and the power rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(11{e}^{x}+8{x}^{2}-12x-20) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(11{e}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8{x}^{2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(12x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(20) \\\\  & =11\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})-12\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(20) \\\\  & =11{e}^{x}+8(2x)-12(1)-0 \\\\  & =11{e}^{x}+16x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={(11{e}^{x}+16x-12)|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =11{e}^{0}+16\\cdot 0-12 \\\\  & =11\\cdot 1+0-12 \\\\  & =11-12 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] ["q-17540" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088059 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abc22f1d-811f-5bdc-b37d-0282e04c8aec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(yx) = x\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085089} {:answer/id #uuid "da5a2b38-cb05-5079-8a67-44b3023a6a33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y\\ln x) = \\ln x\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085090} {:answer/id #uuid "011ca4e6-3122-58c6-a064-72bf61a7cc03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx^{2}}(yx^{2}) = x^{2}\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085091} {:answer/id #uuid "5dc23e01-156d-58f7-838b-e84160a81d5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(\\frac{y}{x}) = \\frac{\\cos x}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085092} {:answer/id #uuid "6436279c-38d0-5c1d-a595-b7ab9c80521e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(ye^{x}) = e^{x}\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085093}] :answer-field/id #uuid "b1c0749d-dee0-5f31-b150-55643e10de7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085088}] :question/id #uuid "c7fefc62-82f5-5578-9142-a780040dc0af" :question/math-academy-id "q-17540" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y = y(x)$:\n$\\frac{dy}{dx} + y = \\cos x$\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{d}{dx}(yI(x)) = I(x)Q(x)$, where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor."}] ["q-272" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060260 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a944189-6813-5164-879c-eab76a5beda0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058183} {:answer/id #uuid "ccc3a755-7484-5e4e-9aa0-2019d5c8e3f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12x^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058184} {:answer/id #uuid "f5bc4c54-58ba-50c8-bfe6-6e8e10018dd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "24x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058185} {:answer/id #uuid "6b798069-ae3e-55a5-aef7-730100f68aa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058186} {:answer/id #uuid "76130876-a748-5eaa-b66a-f6da481d85b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4x^{4}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058187}] :answer-field/id #uuid "be302e32-8941-5ade-84be-3b85b8b0d362" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058182}] :question/id #uuid "4a354b54-aabb-5908-97e9-b4409b8eca72" :question/math-academy-id "q-272" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $f(x) = 4x^{3}$."}] ["q-304035" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297289 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b89210db-d5da-5a48-8355-741becb1873c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "42+\\frac{2}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296232}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296232} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca439fbc-124d-5dae-b8b3-a85cb6575e03" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297054}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0f66d07e-3ca1-595a-b1d7-b4c775329676" :question/math-academy-id "q-304035" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=6{x}^{7}+2{e}^{x}$, the exact value of the slope of the tangent line at $x=-1$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, using the addition and the power rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6{x}^{7}+2{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6{x}^{7})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{7})+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}) \\\\  & =6(7{x}^{6})+2{e}^{x} \\\\  & =42{x}^{6}+2{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=-1} & ={(42{x}^{6}+2{e}^{x})\\,|}_{x=-1} \\\\  & =42(-1)^{6}+2{e}^{-1} \\\\  & =42\\cdot 1+\\frac{2}{e} \\\\  & =42+\\frac{2}{e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] ["q-339949" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314887 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04ee19c8-ffa3-51c2-90c8-f32e76bf3ba8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312005}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312005} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6760650-0666-56ec-a209-471cd8d6b267" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "dffc415e-0ffd-5f91-84e8-ab042b2a6f3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-339949" :question/problem "Given that $y=\\frac{11}{4}ln⁡x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{11}{4}ln⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{4}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] ["q-339950" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314888 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77574496-a3d5-5133-b54d-5a41edeef925" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312931}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312931} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d5f9fb9-2594-5780-812f-98f59dc7cafe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314132}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "eeedc903-d84c-5e00-bc96-dcee7bf9bc01" :question/math-academy-id "q-339950" :question/problem "Given that $y=-\\frac{7}{3}ln⁡x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{7}{3}ln⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{3}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] ["q-340014" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233902 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c8b4247-2f6e-5c89-84d3-05e82fd928d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232814}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186232814} :answer-field/id #uuid "b23a283b-6469-55b9-90b7-faa54b42b98a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232813}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "203042d7-3a90-5b98-a3a8-41d259d10f67" :question/math-academy-id "q-340014" :question/problem "Given the function $y=5{x}^{2}+6\\operatorname{ln}x,$ the slope of the tangent line at $x=3$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{x}^{2}+6\\operatorname{ln}x) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}x) \\\\  & =5\\cdot 2x+6\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =10x+\\frac{6}{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=3$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=3} & ={(10x+\\frac{6}{x})|}_{x=3} \\\\  & =10\\cdot 3+\\frac{6}{3} \\\\  & =32\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] ["q-340056" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314904 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cdb78ad-20bf-5af0-a094-1b3f6357e552" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312717}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312717} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a411b7f-e09b-54e6-9330-1c2c71a4efc6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314334}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6869b95a-63a5-54db-b062-b375ad3ac68d" :question/math-academy-id "q-340056" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=6{e}^{x}+ln⁡8,$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The derivative of ${e}^{x}$ is just ${e}^{x}$ itself. On the other hand, $ln⁡8$ is a constant, so its derivative is $0.$\n\nUsing the addition rule, then, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6{e}^{x}+ln⁡8) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6{e}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡8) \\\\  & =6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+0 \\\\  & =6{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] ["q-340109" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233905 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a68429f7-6205-5d83-9b54-817cfb429a93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3{e}^{2}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232820}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186232820} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb82ad2c-5850-514d-a61d-c6dc21f1e26a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "25397da2-818c-507a-82b9-e23dda017608" :question/math-academy-id "q-340109" :question/problem "Given the function $y=-3{e}^{x}+2{log}_{4}x,$ the slope of the tangent line at $x=2$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-3{e}^{x}+2{log}_{4}x) \\\\  & =-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{4}x) \\\\  & =-3{e}^{x}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}4} \\\\  & =-3{e}^{x}+\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & ={(-3{e}^{x}+\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}4})|}_{x=2} \\\\  & =-3{e}^{2}+\\frac{2}{2\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}4} \\\\  & =-3{e}^{2}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] ["q-340272" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314919 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "202a3876-df45-5f69-9dea-3b48cc477974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}(8){8}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312218}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312218} :answer-field/id #uuid "5168e7a2-5958-57af-b48a-ff61e1073f47" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314237}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ca876738-9b8d-5832-85d7-2d09df78130a" :question/math-academy-id "q-340272" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=7-2\\cdot {8}^{x}$, find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7-2\\cdot {8}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\cdot {8}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7)-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({8}^{x}) \\\\  & =0-2(ln⁡(8){8}^{x}) \\\\  & =-2ln⁡(8){8}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] ["q-340280" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314920 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40066746-e699-53ed-82fd-0f35f8e924c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}(5)+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312491}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312491} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4ba52fe-3ccd-59f7-bca4-208b03b18375" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314595}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d2b3624c-f62d-5f81-b0de-c13d8e4bf17c" :question/math-academy-id "q-340280" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={5}^{x}-6{x}^{3}+4x-1$, the slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({5}^{x}-6{x}^{3}+4x-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({5}^{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6{x}^{3})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({5}^{x})-6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})+4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\  & =ln⁡(5)\\cdot {5}^{x}-6(3{x}^{2})+4(1)-0 \\\\  & =ln⁡(5)\\cdot {5}^{x}-18{x}^{2}+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={(ln⁡(5)\\cdot {5}^{x}-18{x}^{2}+4)|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =ln⁡(5)\\cdot {5}^{0}-18(0)^{2}+4 \\\\  & =ln⁡(5)\\cdot 1-0+4 \\\\  & =ln⁡(5)+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] ["q-342663" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317308 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afdc11cd-82dd-5c6f-bcb3-29722512bae8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316117}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316117} :answer-field/id #uuid "466922a0-7e46-579f-8acd-8a627c38b832" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316705}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4d9eda9c-9861-5891-97dc-ba4b870f7db4" :question/math-academy-id "q-342663" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={(3x+1)}^{4},$ the slope at the point $(-1,16)$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use chain rule to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\nFirst, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf={g}^{4},\\,g=3x+1\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=4{g}^{3},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =4{g}^{3}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =12(3x+1{)}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line at the point where $x=-1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=-1} & =[12(3x+1{)}^{3}{]}_{x=-1} \\\\  & =12(3\\cdot (-1)+1{)}^{3} \\\\  & =12(-2{)}^{3} \\\\  & =-96.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] ["q-48625" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097250 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85752216-72d1-52c5-a307-1f7593bb2baa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2(x^{4} + 3x)(4x^{3} + 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095425} {:answer/id #uuid "bffd2b2f-d555-5e17-8756-8a754febf526" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2(x^{4} + 3x)(4x^{3} + 3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095426} {:answer/id #uuid "eef892e3-6947-592f-9345-311b595e0536" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2(4x^{3})(x^{4} + 3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095427} {:answer/id #uuid "05327ffd-b783-558f-8116-edad45453171" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2(4x^{3})(x^{4} + 3x)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095428} {:answer/id #uuid "62baa9f7-a4b9-5ff4-84f6-37fdf189f3fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2(x^{4} + 3x)(4x^{3} + 3)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095429}] :answer-field/id #uuid "a72fa786-3004-51a5-a233-17a9a216dfb3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095424}] :question/id #uuid "b551e489-4c37-53ea-831b-8f3ca007450b" :question/math-academy-id "q-48625" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{df}{dx}$ when $f(x) = (x^{4} + 3x)^{2}$."}] ["q-49942" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097290 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9acd2481-0ec3-5994-9168-964cb3c474c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(x) = \\frac{1}{2}e^{x} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095665} {:answer/id #uuid "b3631b1e-e008-5fb9-a825-84c8ecba10b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(x) = e^{x} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095666} {:answer/id #uuid "c508b657-4c25-56c5-960c-217135f76315" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(x) =-\\frac{1}{2}e^{x} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095667} {:answer/id #uuid "f83fba29-574c-5d24-b1a6-4adbe9283fcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(x) = \\frac{1}{2}(e^{x} - 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095668} {:answer/id #uuid "38b83252-dae4-5abd-841f-1818a0da90fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(x) =-\\frac{1}{2}(e^{x} + 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095669}] :answer-field/id #uuid "62dcfac4-1b46-5254-bc04-921bedd65cbf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095664}] :question/id #uuid "36f54028-9879-56b6-bec9-c97cd80fb58e" :question/math-academy-id "q-49942" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation below that satisfies the condition $f(0) =-1$.\n\n$2f^{′}(x) + e^{x} = 0$."}] ["q-50136" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097299 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07a181c2-eaa7-54a0-8890-e935b4d4ff1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{2x}-2{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330015} {:answer/id #uuid "15c676e1-03b3-5352-b3b8-1386a7ac7b2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{2x}-{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330129} {:answer/id #uuid "c78be5e7-440c-5080-aede-7717891b5955" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{2x}-{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331715} {:answer/id #uuid "cdb467dd-d851-57e6-ba23-4d6c40542276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{2x}-2{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331773} {:answer/id #uuid "fd0ac1c2-8887-5016-9ea9-5bc26155b0dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-4{e}^{2x}-2{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332172}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330129} :answer-field/id #uuid "7491e487-3ec6-578a-921d-573211c3741a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332412}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "cb82aa2f-3e4a-523a-94c2-c95aa3cb8ffa" :question/math-academy-id "q-50136" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4{e}^{2x}=-2x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate the derivative term:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-4{e}^{2x}-2x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-4{e}^{2x}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int (-4{e}^{2x}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}y & =\\int (-4{e}^{2x}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-4\\int {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2x}-{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] ["q-50139" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097300 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89aee0c2-41c4-50d9-95e7-d07999f8e43b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y = 5x^{2} + Cx + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095725} {:answer/id #uuid "a8264bab-88eb-5c1b-8cf6-4b5658e50c5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y = Cx^{2} + 10x + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095726} {:answer/id #uuid "c8066636-9a63-5ade-85aa-07f7e0be5cab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y =-5x^{2} + Cx + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095727} {:answer/id #uuid "0a099fae-b25d-5abb-a50a-c5dc1eda7e34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y =-5x^{2} + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095728} {:answer/id #uuid "1a40f9c2-33a9-5233-bec8-c51acd272979" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y =-5x^{2} + Cx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095729}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8c860608-75a8-5451-a1a7-a0683cdbc84f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095724} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29a4235d-41c9-5a0e-b658-3ec6b027584e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-5{x}^{2}+Cx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398891} {:answer/id #uuid "4b317621-35b4-53d1-939d-fab67d8f1031" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-5{x}^{2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398892} {:answer/id #uuid "6dcf3415-556b-53c7-ac6f-21a5ddefd845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-5{x}^{2}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398893} {:answer/id #uuid "a552a9bb-4de8-5448-90ec-372d3554e55d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=5{x}^{2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398894} {:answer/id #uuid "fa85c5fe-d852-5230-88fd-53d91e4bcd53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=C{x}^{2}+10x+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398895}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398892} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1789600-f409-5b68-8f83-26b29073f519" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398890}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "17751a3b-ed4b-5966-a450-330460c02715" :question/math-academy-id "q-50139" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=-10.$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =-10\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-10x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-10x+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-10\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+Cx+D \\\\  & =-5{x}^{2}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"}] ["q-50148" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097301 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a745d53-2adc-5935-a97d-5a586599fa37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y =-\\frac{1}{3}e^{3x} + Cx + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095731} {:answer/id #uuid "f4387418-5075-52c7-b685-924f2791a4be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y = \\frac{1}{9}e^{3x} + Cx^{2} + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095732} {:answer/id #uuid "035eddbc-75fb-53ba-bc61-c5e0c4f3f025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y = \\frac{1}{9}e^{3x} + Cx + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095733} {:answer/id #uuid "12887777-c8a6-5e16-bf30-ed290559c1e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y =-\\frac{1}{9}e^{3x} + Cx^{2} + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095734} {:answer/id #uuid "7a68fbfe-8f1c-512a-8cc2-1b00fe18af49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y = \\frac{1}{3}e^{3x} + Cx + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095735}] :answer-field/id #uuid "1b5a4615-20d2-563a-8738-3f3905aa1549" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095730} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae67e9eb-7a6a-5f1f-9633-a869be11af9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{3x}+C{x}^{2}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398897} {:answer/id #uuid "1e9d1539-56f7-56d2-9de6-1e9901343c60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398898} {:answer/id #uuid "fb9ac46a-1dd6-5423-b497-fd6f6d213a70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{3x}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398899} {:answer/id #uuid "bd19773a-598c-5d4a-9935-ec0892a47ffb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398900} {:answer/id #uuid "89be7220-c09b-594d-8bff-c3a06f0b9221" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{3x}+C{x}^{2}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398901}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398899} :answer-field/id #uuid "30eeac9f-d833-5bc8-934f-4097337092f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398896}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3e04bc45-f34f-56fc-9a0e-8643597c4852" :question/math-academy-id "q-50148" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-{e}^{3x}=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{1}{3}\\,{e}^{3x})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{3x}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"}] ["q-50195" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097302 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "853aeea8-65f0-5fb9-8258-80667aea2abd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/8b/8bd666d1415f83ff8232e39963248ef0afe62f39e66d5f3416ae18316453faa3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095737} {:answer/id #uuid "a94dc35e-7f42-58d5-bacb-d6ebe1a5ec26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/0a/0ab0b12088ac6816f7086e952e749ea6d4c9107cc6189ebb0efcafb904152ad0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095738} {:answer/id #uuid "efb18e51-9c8d-5683-8dc6-f9dd9a0e7082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/1a/1a0e6d6d025e2f8b79019036637efd78b89954d1b01b00037ece77df4c3844eb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095739} {:answer/id #uuid "fa9b1208-989e-52fe-9319-003ca0fe7916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/65/65ae1770ff4084d5a89fdda0f552f2a92380ae948c2b0f1ef3d3bb5d20f32713.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095740} {:answer/id #uuid "3c3f4a30-dc1d-5668-a728-9b3bc043b41c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/5d/5d686380cd025e83e38524918c5cfaf215726f0f0d05783b8f88fd5f281c091c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095741}] :answer-field/id #uuid "baa5bcf1-a2e1-5611-80a8-e28d46985c9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answ